There's a hint of nostolgia in Crosscode which brings me back to the earlier years of video gaming.  There's always something new to look forward too when there are updates.
Pros:
- Parkour in each area;
- The Combat system is enjoyable;
- AI is good and complements the gameplay;
- Exploration leads to hidden items and for item completion;
- Gamepad works wonders and is calibrated effectively;
- Boss battles are challenging, requiring thinking and quick reactions;
- The puzzles are interesting and challenging;
- Storyline is great and characters are enjoyable
- Menu feature is great
Cons:
- Some puzzles require tutorials that have not given in-depth explanations.
Other than that, this game is amazing and would recommend this to people who are yearning for a nostolgic type game from the SNES.

